    "title": "Old Vestal Fire Station demolition to finish tomorrow - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jim Ehmke ,\n7 hours ago\nVESTAL, N.Y. (WIVT/WBGH) – Just east on the Parkway, one of the older buildings in Vestal is also coming down.\nMarchuska Brothers Construction is demolishing the former Vestal Fire Station No. 4.\nThe station was vacated a couple years ago when the fire department built a new structure behind Kohl’s Department Store where the Vestal American Legion once stood.\nIn April, the fire department sold the property to Marchuska Development for $900,000.\nDemolition of the structure is expected to be finished tomorrow\nJustin Marchuska tells News 34 that his company is considering splitting the parcel into two pads.\nHe says they’re still looking for partners interested in developing the site.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WIVT - News 34.",
    "summary": "Marchuska Brothers Construction is demolishing the former Vestal Fire Station No. The station was vacated a couple years ago when the fire department built a new structure behind Kohl’s Department Store where the Vestal American Legion once stood. In April, the fire department sold the property to Marchuska Development for $900,000. Demolition of the structure is expected to be finished tomorrow Justin Marchuska tells News 34 that his company is considering splitting the parcel into two pads. Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved.",
